# Thumbnail and title rules (25 Sep 2026)

Readable copy with the evidence: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/THUMBNAIL_AND_TITLE_RULES.md`.

## Titles

- A familiar noun in the first four words (your hands, your bones, a table, a drop of water, you).
- One concrete promise: a familiar thing turned strange; the body or the everyday seen for the first time; a yes/no about what everyone believed; a prediction that came true; one real number or object; an accident that changed everything.
- Longs: the searched phrase, subject in the first five words, the thing over the method. Not *How Did We Discover X?* every week.
- **FAIL:** abstract labels or riddles (*What other table has empty chairs?* 4 views), hedged claims, hashtags, series suffixes, a copy of a live title, fear framing. Under about 60 characters.

## Long thumbs

- One subject filling at least a third of the frame, simple warm background.
- **2–4 words**, readable at 168×94: `python3 00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/thumb_preview.py long <thumb> --out <sheet>`.
- The thumb adds to the title, never repeats it. One heavy capitals font, yellow hook word, white rest. Text off the subject and out of the bottom-right corner.
- The Explorer only as a tested variant. Test & Compare with 3; judge CTR past about 500 impressions.

## Shorts

- **Frame 0 is the thumbnail in the feed:** the named thing, moving. Never the Explorer, a blank card grid or a dark card.
- Frame-0 caption: the promise in 2–4 words, cap height about 8–10%, yellow hook word.
- Custom cover: the title's hook words, 2–4 words, at least 60% of frame width, vertically centred. Check with `thumb_preview.py short`.
